robin <usenet@unrated.net> wrote:

>First, I want to thank everyone who participated (players, coders ad 
>administrators); the Tournament couldn't happen without everyone's 
>contributions.

(1) Thanks to the organisers!

(2) Congratulations to the big achievers! Congratulations to anyone who
ascended! Congratulations to anyone who achieved a personal best!

(3) Allowing FTP access for transmitting .nethackrc would be very useful.
Alterrnatively, a simple web form allowing to upload such files would
also work. There is no pressing need for implementing editor access on
the servers.

(4) I liked the new challenge. Granted, I did not run into the troubles
that other people faced, such as examining the inventory taking up turns
with respect to the grue counter. I am in favour of adding new secret,
voluntary challenges.

(5) You should filter your patches through more experienced patchers
before deploying them in the tournament. I am sure that there are several
capable people in rgrn willing to help.

(6) I support that there are several trophies valueing high scores. I
agree that a 8,000,000-points ascension speaks in general for a less
skilled ascension than a 2,000,000-points ascension, but it /is/ the
/score/ system of NetHack. It is the job of the DevTeam to come up with a
score system, and they choose this one. So we should take it. There is
enough room for other valuations of skill, as exhibited by other
trophies.

(7) I am looking forward to next November.

